[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m [response] The area of a triangle with vertices at the origin \(O(0,0,0)\), \(A(x_1, y_1, z_1)\), and \(B(x_2, y_2, z_2)\) can be found using the cross product of the vectors \(\overrightarrow{OA}\) and \(\overrightarrow{OB}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m The formula for the area of the triangle is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \| \overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} \| \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \overrightarrow{OA} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m The cross product \(\overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB}\) is calculated as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\ -3 & -2 & 1 \end{vmatrix} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ = \mathbf{i}(2 \cdot 1 - 3 \cdot (-2)) - \mathbf{j}(1 \cdot 1 - 3 \cdot (-3)) + \mathbf{k}(1 \cdot (-2) - 2 \cdot (-3)) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ = \mathbf{i}(2 + 6) - \mathbf{j}(1 + 9) + \mathbf{k}(-2 + 6) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ = 8\mathbf{i} - 10\mathbf{j} + 4\mathbf{k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ -10 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m The magnitude of this cross product vector is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \| \overrightarrow{OA} \times \overrightarrow{OB} \| = \sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \sqrt{180} = 6\sqrt{5} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m So the area of the triangle \(OAB\) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m \[ \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 6\sqrt{5} = 3\sqrt{5} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2696761)[0m import numpy as np
